{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggJSNeAPHefPKVVYix8j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hotfix is in `money.py`, and the tests pass. I did not commit or push.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` used `total // people` and gave every person that share, so the remainder was dropped. `split_cents(100, 3)` returned `[33, 33, 33]`.\n\n**The fix:** `divmod` splits the total, and the first `remainder` people each get one extra grosz:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, and the shares always sum to the total.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_remainder_goes_to_first_people_so_total_is_preserved` to `test_money.py` before changing the code. It failed on the old code with `[33, 33, 33] != [34, 33, 33]`. After the fix, all 4 tests pass with `python3 -m unittest test_money`.\n\nI kept the test in this change, so the regression is covered now. That's a few lines, which fits the deploy window. Pyflakes isn't installed here, so I didn't run a linter.\n\nDecision for you: the extra grosz goes to the first people in the list. If the payment flow needs a different rule, such as the payer absorbing it, tell me and I'll change it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":924,"cache_read_input_tokens":21703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":924},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efb5ba68-c506-453c-9922-00919205a400","uuid":"5d46d0b2-20b1-4d2c-aa15-0186e3447b63","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:21:46.839Z","request_id":"req_011CggJSNRWnbEUVwawky1y2"}
